Build qemu:


git clone https://github.com/qemu/qemu.git
cd qemu
git submodule update --init --recursive


mkdir build && cd build
../configure --target-list=x86_64-softmmu
ninja



Build buildroot:

make qemu_x86_64_defconfig
make -j$(nproc)

(deselect host qemu in  make menuconfig)




start qemu:

/build/qemu-system-x86_64 \
  -M q35 \
  -m 512M \
  -enable-kvm \
  -device mynet-pci \
  -kernel buildroot/output/images/bzImage \
  -drive file=buildroot/output/images/rootfs.ext2,if=virtio,format=raw \
  -append "root=/dev/vda console=ttyS0" \
  -nographic


./qemu-system-x86_64 \
  -M q35 \
  -m 512M \
  -enable-kvm \
  -device mynet-pci \
  -kernel ~/Developer/buildroot/output/images/bzImage \
  -drive file=~/Developer/buildroot/output/images/rootfs.ext2,if=virtio,format=raw \
  -append "root=/dev/vda console=ttyS0" \
  -fsdev local,id=fsdev0,path=/home/minimoog/Developer/qemu-pcie-net/linux-driver,security_model=none \
  -device virtio-9p-pci,fsdev=fsdev0,mount_tag=hostshare \
  -nographic


  Add to buildroot config:

  Symbol: NET_9P [=n]
Type  : tristate
Prompt: Plan 9 Resource Sharing Support (9P2000)
  Location:
    -> Networking support (NET [=y])
      -> Networking options
Symbol: 9P_FS [=y]
  Location:
    -> File systems
      -> Network File Systems (NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS [=y])
Symbol: NET_9P_VIRTIO [=n]
  Depends on: NET_9P [=n] && VIRTIO


Mount shared directory in qemu and insmod the driver:

mkdir -p /mnt/host
mount -t 9p -o trans=virtio,version=9p2000.L hostshare /mnt/host
insmod /mnt/host/mynet_drv.ko



